{#
    The hidden fields FormSubmissionHandler reads, plus the honeypot and the
    anchor the post-submission redirect points at.

    One include instead of five things to remember: the CSRF token under the id
    the bundle declares stateless, the page to return to, the rank of this form
    block, a honeypot, and a marker to scroll back to. Getting any of them
    subtly wrong is what copying a controller and its template into each project
    used to cost.

    Put it right inside the <form> element, before the visible fields:

        <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_contact_send') }}" class="iw-form iw-form__grid">
            {% include '@ItechWorldSuluTailwindTheme/forms/_fields.html.twig' with {
                formIndex: formIndex|default(1)
            } only %}
            …

    Parameters:
      - formIndex: rank of the form block in the page, as handed to the included
                   template by the form block. Defaults to 1, which is what a
                   template included outside the block gets.

    Override it in your project at the standard Symfony bundle path:
    templates/bundles/ItechWorldSuluTailwindThemeBundle/forms/_fields.html.twig
#}

{% set index = formIndex|default(1) %}

{# The token is validated without a session: the form lives in a page served
   from a seven-day proxy cache, where a session-bound token would be the one of
   whoever warmed that cache. The id is declared stateless by the bundle itself,
   so there is nothing to configure in the project. #}
<input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value="{{ csrf_token('iw_form') }}">

{# Where to send the visitor back. pathInfo only: the handler refuses anything
   that is not an absolute path of this site anyway. #}
<input type="hidden" name="_redirect" value="{{ app.request.pathInfo }}">

<input type="hidden" name="_form_index" value="{{ index }}">

{# Honeypot: hidden from sight, from the keyboard and from screen readers. A
   submission that fills it in is answered as a success and sent nowhere. #}
<div hidden aria-hidden="true">
    <label for="iw-form-website-{{ index }}">{{ 'iw_sulu_tailwind_theme.form_honeypot_label'|trans }}</label>
    <input type="text" id="iw-form-website-{{ index }}" name="_iw_website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
</div>

{# Anchor target of the redirect, so the visitor lands on the form rather than
   at the top of a long page. Rendered here rather than expected on the <form>
   element: the handler builds the anchor on its own and cannot know what id a
   project gave its form. #}
<span id="iw-form-block-{{ index }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
